    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>1. The sphere is centered at the origin and it has radius <m>2</m>. Thus it matches A.</p>
<p>2. Completing the squares, yields <m>(x-1)^2+(y+1)^2+(z-1)^2 = 1</m>. Thus the sphere is centered at <m>(1,-1,1)</m> and has radius <m>1</m>.
Its graph matches  E.</p>
<p>3. Completing the squares, yields <m>(x-2)^2+y^2+z^2 = \frac{1}{4}</m>. Thus the sphere is centered at <m>(2,0,0)</m> and has radius <m>\frac{1}{2}</m>.
Its graph matches  F.</p>
<p>4. Completing the squares, yields <m>(x-2)^2+(y-2)^2+(z-1)^2 = \frac{1}{4}</m>. Thus the sphere is centered at <m>(2,2,1)</m> and has radius <m>\frac{1}{2}</m>.
Its graph matches  D.</p>
</solution>
